 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Passkey account preview
+
+The home page and `/devtools-times/account/security` expose the new security settings. The original news home is available at `/devtools-times/news`.
+
+The account preview is isolated per server-side Astro session and starts with three clearly labeled example passkeys. Renaming and removing passkeys persist in that session. New passkeys use native WebAuthn with `@simplewebauthn/server` verification, a short-lived single-use challenge, required user verification, and discoverable credentials. Credential public keys stay server-side. Mutations require a matching Origin header. Password-manager synchronization is feature-detected; example credentials are never sent to the password manager.
+
+This is a demo account, not an authenticated production account. Before production use, replace the session-created demo identity with the app’s authenticated user, store credentials in the account database, implement assertion verification for passkey sign-in, and require reauthentication for sensitive account changes. The existing external sign-in form does not currently establish an authenticated session in this app. Device registration requires HTTPS or localhost. The Node adapter’s default filesystem session driver is intended for this local preview; use shared persistent session storage in a multi-instance deployment.
+
+Validation: `pnpm build`, then start the app with `pnpm start` and run `pnpm check:passkeys` in another terminal. API checks cover session isolation, rename/delete persistence, input validation, origin checks, registration options, and rejection of invalid registration responses. Actual device enrollment requires an authenticator and was not manually verified in a browser.
